It doesn't seem straightforward to add a proper test case for this in rustc, which may also explain why the similar [AArch64 patch](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/commit/ebcbcc8b73cb6fa8aad42e258ca0382db68e7876) didn't include one. One of the goals of this patch is to fix the issue that prevents miri from working on LoongArch, where the default jemalloc page size fails to meet the requirements and causes an assertion failure:

https://github.com/tikv/jemalloc/blob/09ad115bc02db60cc9d9338cf0067074d3135fb4/src/pages.c#L759-L766

```c
	os_page = os_page_detect();
	if (os_page > PAGE) {
		malloc_write("<jemalloc>: Unsupported system page size\n");
		if (opt_abort) {
			abort();
		}
		return true;
	}
```

